{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Cast.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Push"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.signedCumulant_eq_neg_one_pow_mul_cumulant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.signedCumulant_eq_neg_one_pow_mul_cumulant","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L126-L133","doc":"The same statement for the unsigned coefficients, since that is the form the\nmeasured table is quoted in: `μ_k` alternates, and it is `(-1)^k μ_k` whose second\ndifference must vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.not_affine_of_secondDiff_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.not_affine_of_secondDiff_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L114-L124","doc":"**The contrapositive: one non-zero second difference refutes the entire affine\nclass.**\n\n`s` is the observed signed-coefficient sequence.  If any single second difference\nof it is non-zero, then no `(α, β)` whatsoever generates it — so the exclusion\nneeds no fit, and no search over parameters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.secondDiff_signedCumulant_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.secondDiff_signedCumulant_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L106-L112","doc":"**The second difference vanishes identically, for every `(α, β)`.**\n\nThis is the invariant the exclusion rests on, and it is why the test is\nparameter-free: `α` and `β` have cancelled before any measured value is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.signedCumulant_succ_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.signedCumulant_succ_sub","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L100-L104","doc":"**The signed coefficient is affine in `k`** — the content of the whole file,\nstated as a one-step difference that does not depend on `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_five","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L93-L96","doc":"`μ₅ = B(5) − 5·B(4) + 10·B(3) − 10·B(2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_four","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L88-L91","doc":"`μ₄ = B(4) − 4·B(3) + 6·B(2)` — matches `CoordinationWeightDifferences.b4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_three_eq_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_three_eq_neg","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L85-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_three","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L79-L83","doc":"`μ₃ = B(3) − 3·B(2)`, and this equals `−(3α + 2β)` — the value\n`AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.b3_affine_eq` proves independently. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant_two","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L75-L77","doc":"`μ₂ = B(2)` — matches `CoordinationWeightDifferences` with `B 0 = B 1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.cumulant","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L70-L71","doc":"The binomial-basis coefficient itself, `μ_k = (-1)^k · signedCumulant`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.signedCumulant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.signedCumulant","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L66-L68","doc":"The **signed** binomial-basis coefficient, `(-1)^k μ_k`, under the affine ansatz.\nThe claim of this file is that *this* is the affine object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.bind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.AffineCumulantSecondDifference.bind","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/AffineCumulantSecondDifference.lean#L62-L64","doc":"The affine count multiplicity `μ(A) = α·A + β`, matching\n`AffineCountMultiplicityWindow.mu`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}